From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: valentin rameau <valentin.rameau@outlook.fr>
Date: Sat, 19 Sep 2026 23:17:36 +0900
Subject: [PATCH 21/33] Hoist the widescreen-HUD test out of the compose loop

compose is the largest PPU phase on Vita (5137 us/frame, 41% of the measured
rasteriser). Its per-pixel body recomputed a blanking test that depends only
on i and on booleans already fixed for the scanline:

  outside_world = i < hud_world_left || i >= hud_world_right
  keep_hud      = three comparisons against main_layer

All three *_full_width flags require ppu->extraLeftRight to be nonzero, and
with widescreen off hud_world is [272, 528) while the window span is exactly
272..528 -- so the test can never blank a pixel, yet paid two range checks per
pixel plus, in the no-math loop, a nibble extract and three comparisons.

Decided once per window span into hud_checks_needed. Behind
g_ppu_fast_compose so it can be A/B'd on device.

Also un-gates g_ppu_fast_sprite_eval from __vita__ so PC can verify it too.
Both paths are now proven pixel-exact: byte-identical framebuffer hashes over
3999 frames spanning 2520 distinct images.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
